{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-105882",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $T$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $T$ where every element of $T$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,10},{2,4,6,8}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{0,2,4,6,8},{10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,2,4,6,8,10,12}}$ is not a partition because the element $12$ does not appear in $T.$\n\n- ${{0,10},{2},{4,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $6\\in T$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{0,10},{2,4,6,8,10}}$ is not a partition because the element $10$ appears in two subsets.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
